{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfgSUD9gtuqDstJR4VkdT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the plan and saved both files in the folder:\n\n- **`plan.md`**: the plan you can read. It's a 3×3 grid (Before / During / After, each with three steps) plus a short block underneath with the monthly budget, the weekly time split, what to check each month, what to say no to, and my assumptions.\n- **`plan.csv`**: the same grid as exactly 3 rows × 3 columns, ready for Google Sheets (File → Import). Each cell starts with its stage, for example \"[DURING] Get their contact…\". I read the file back after saving and it opens correctly as a 3×3 grid.\n\n**The main ideas:**\n1. **Stop losing the people who ask about classes at the fair.** Replace \"follow me on Instagram\" with a QR code on the stall and in every mug bag. It opens WhatsApp with a message already written (\"quiero info de las clases\"). Switch to WhatsApp Business so you can label contacts, and keep all leads in one Google Sheet.\n2. **Run the taster on a fixed date each month, then follow up the same evening.** People who sign up for the monthly class within 7 days get their taster fee counted toward it.\n3. **Open the Wednesday group with \"founding member\" deposits.** Start it once 4 people have paid. The target is Wed 4 Nov. If 4 haven't paid by 28 Oct, keep the list and launch in March.\n4. **Fight \"my schedule changed\".** Let students switch between Saturday and Wednesday, give one make-up class a month, and offer a 3-month pass.\n5. **Turn word of mouth into a simple offer.** The friend gets half off the taster, and the student who brought them gets a free mug once the friend finishes their first month.\n\nIt all fits your 5 hours a week and ARS 70,000 a month.\n\n**My assumptions (you should check these):**\n- The costs for printing and for promoting the best Reel on Instagram are estimates.\n- I made up the prices for the 3-month pass and the discounts, so compare them with your costs.\n- I expect January to be slow because people leave the city.\n- I assumed one Wednesday group can mix Spanish and English speakers.\n- I told you to say no to café wholesale and international shipping.\n\nI didn't install anything or send anything to an outside service."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":685,"cache_read_input_tokens":26388,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":685},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e7b2c35-8d3b-426a-b29c-70724907ffdf","uuid":"1c8e0513-07da-4bc8-ac96-526642a6c1ed","timestamp":"2026-10-04T02:52:42.759Z","request_id":"req_011CfgSUCrKUiHdy6PMJGN72"}
